=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# users refusals -----------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: The refusals before asking, each from the real reading:$
# the item, the host, the user.$
$
# remove, hardn, george ----------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# You're running hardn through george's sudo. Removing it would$
# leave no way to become root. Grant another user first.$
$
# remove, debian13, george -------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# george is an admin through /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users,$
# which hardn didn't write, so hardn can't remove it. Change it$
# there.$
$
# remove, debian13, alice --------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# alice is an admin through the sudo group, which hardn leaves$
# alone. Take alice out of it with gpasswd -d alice sudo.$
$
# remove, legacy, george ---------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# george is an admin through /etc/sudoers.d/george, which hardn$
# didn't write, so hardn can't remove it. Change it there.$
$
# remove, alpine323, george ------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# george is an admin through the wheel group, which hardn leaves$
# alone. Take george out of it with gpasswd -d george wheel.$
$
# remove, not-read, george -------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't read sudo's rules: its files don't check. Check$
# them with visudo -c, then try again.$
$
# require, debian13, george ------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# george has no password, so sudo couldn't ask for one. Set one$
# with passwd george, then try again.$
$
# require, alpine323, george -----------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# george has no password, so doas couldn't ask for one. Set one$
# with passwd george, then try again.$
$
# remove-key, one-key, george ----------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# This is george's last key, and you're logged in as george. Add$
# another key first.$
$
# grant, no-sudo, george ---------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# sudo isn't installed, so hardn can't grant admin rights.$
# Install sudo, then try again.$
$
# grant, not-read, alice ---------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't read sudo's rules: its files don't check. Check$
# them with visudo -c, then try again.$
$
# remove, root-login, george -----------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't tell who you're logged in as, and george is the$
# last admin. Grant another user first.$
$
# remove-key, alpine-stray, george -----------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# This is george's last key, and you're logged in as george. Add$
# another key first.$
$
# add-key, group-home, alice -----------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# sshd would ignore a key for alice: /home/alice is writable by$
# its group (0775). With StrictModes it takes keys only where$
# the home and ~/.ssh are the user's own and no one else can$
# write to them.$
$
$

